index 34d81594b36e558f7bb0a8beb0c4cce7ad50beab..54d0a069c9b9e859ba31184dc89dc99eb422bf7f 100644
--- a/docs/csv_export.rst
+++ b/docs/csv_export.rst
@@ -45,6 +45,24 @@ The following options can be used to customize the CSVs returned by Datasette.
 ``?_dl=on``
     Causes Datasette to return a ``content-disposition: attachment; filename="filename.csv"`` header.
 
+``?_null=TEXT``
+    Use ``TEXT`` to represent SQL ``NULL`` values. For example,
+    ``/database/table.csv?_null=NULL`` exports them as ``NULL`` instead of empty
+    fields. Omitting this parameter, or passing an explicit empty value with
+    ``?_null=``, keeps the default output. Non-NULL values, including empty
+    strings and the number ``0``, are unchanged.
+
+    This option works for table and custom SQL query exports, on every page of
+    a ``_stream=1`` export, and with ``_header=off``. With ``_labels=1``, a NULL
+    foreign key uses the marker in both its value and label columns. A label
+    that is itself SQL NULL also uses the marker; a real empty string label
+    remains empty.
+
+    URL-encode the text when using Unicode or special characters in the query
+    string. Commas, quotes and line breaks in the marker are escaped using the
+    usual CSV quoting rules. The marker is also HTML-escaped in ``_trace=1``
+    debug output. This option only affects CSV exports, not JSON row data.
+
 Streaming all records
